From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:06:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: aop_als: arm the sensor again after a system
 sleep

A system sleep stops the AOP's endpoints, and the CT817 comes back with
its report interval at zero. It reports only on the zero to non-zero
transition that enable_als() makes at probe, so after the first deep
sleep the ambient-light reading keeps its last value for the rest of the
boot. On the J700 that was 80 identical readings over 20 s while the
sensor was covered and then lit; rebinding the driver restored it.

Do what the temperature service already does: set the interval to zero
when a sleep is prepared and run the probe's arming sequence again after
it. Leave the interval at zero on unbind too, so that a later probe arms
the sensor.

Tested on the J700 (T8140): the module rebuilt against the running
kernel and loaded in place of the old one, then one deep sleep. Covered
and lit afterwards, the sensor read 0.77 to 5211 lux, 40 distinct
readings in 80.

Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit f3b5aa437975ae9d41520cf15f9a94080e84e35b)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs | 202 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 183 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs b/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
index e64f7ff26a..ff2ef90f56 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
@@ -4,15 +4,24 @@
 //!
